  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "Collectively, the records show that heating HEAs can produce lattice disorder or melting, composition-dependent diffusion, surface enrichment or depletion, and preferential outward transport associated with diffusivity or volatility. They therefore point toward thermally activated, nonuniform elemental redistribution. However, none studies AuCoCuNiPt nanoparticles or identifies surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation under vacuum, nanoparticle reshaping-enhanced diffusion, or subsequent evaporation and size-distribution changes. Reconstructing the specific in situ nanoparticle-heating intervention and its coupled segregation–reshaping–evaporation mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
